### TaskMaster API - sample requests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### After register/login, paste the token into @token below.

@base = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### 1. Register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Alice", "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 2. Login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 3. My profile
GET {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3b. Update profile
PATCH {{base}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bio": "Backend developer", "name": "Alice W" }

### 11. Create a team (note the inviteCode in the response)
POST {{base}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Backend Squad", "description": "API work" }

### 11b. Join a team with an invite code (use a second user's token)
POST {{base}}/teams/join
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "inviteCode": "PASTE_CODE" }

### 11c. Invite an existing user by email
POST {{base}}/teams/1/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com" }

### 4. Create a task
POST {{base}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Write API docs", "description": "Document every endpoint", "dueDate": "2026-12-31", "priority": "high", "teamId": 1 }

### 5. Tasks assigned to me
GET {{base}}/tasks?assignee=me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Filter by status
GET {{base}}/tasks?status=open&sortBy=dueDate&order=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Search
GET {{base}}/tasks?search=docs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Assign task 1 to user 2
POST {{base}}/tasks/1/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": 2 }

### 6. Mark completed
POST {{base}}/tasks/1/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Add a comment
POST {{base}}/tasks/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "content": "Started working on this" }

### 10b. Upload an attachment (multipart)
POST {{base}}/tasks/1/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary

------Boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello from the attachment
------Boundary--

### Task detail (includes comments + attachments)
GET {{base}}/tasks/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Notifications
GET {{base}}/notifications?unread=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13b. Live stream (SSE) - keeps the connection open
GET {{base}}/notifications/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. AI description
POST {{base}}/ai/describe
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Set up CI pipeline", "notes": "GitHub Actions, run tests on every PR" }

### 12. Logout
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
